[1m[38;5;231mHow long should the stored identity live?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153msessionStorage (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSurvives page reloads and navigation between pages, cleared when the tab closes. No expiry logic needed. Fits a [39m
     [38;5;246mmulti-page app with no backend.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m localStorage
     [38;5;246mSurvives browser restart. Adds an expiry and invalidation story, and widens the window where a stale identity can [39m
     [38;5;246mlinger.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m In-memory only
     [38;5;246mA variable in a session module. Simplest and no storage exposure, but lost on every page load — likely breaks the [39m
     [38;5;246mmulti-page case.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m httpOnly cookie
     [38;5;246mMost resistant to XSS since JS cannot read it, but requires standing up the backend that API_ENDPOINT only stubs [39m
     [38;5;246mtoday. Larger scope.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
